WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.938
Everything in Intune starts with
the trusted certificate profile.

2
00:00:03.938 --> 00:00:07.546
It puts the root and issuing
CA certificates on the device,

3
00:00:07.546 --> 00:00:09.576
so the device can build the chain.

4
00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:13.488
If the device doesn't trust the
root, every other profile fails.

5
00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:15.563
Then there are three delivery paths.

6
00:00:15.563 --> 00:00:19.259
SCEP with Cloud PKI, where
the device makes its own key,

7
00:00:19.259 --> 00:00:24.300
contrary to what the old guide said,
and no on-premises servers are needed.

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.302
SCEP with AD CS, which runs through
NDES and the Intune connector,

9
00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:32.700
with the key still never
leaving the device.

10
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:38.375
And PKCS, where the connector generates the
key on its own server and hands it over.

11
00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:43.662
That means the private key exists, however
briefly, somewhere other than the device.

12
00:00:43.662 --> 00:00:47.660
That trade is why the program
prefers SCEP wherever it can.
